Delete Head of Doubly Linked List — Quick Revision

To delete the head, first handle the edge cases: if head == null or the list has only one node (head.next == null), return null. Otherwise, move head to head.next and set head.prev = null to remove the backward link to the deleted node. Finally, return the new head.

Key idea: In a doubly linked list, when the head is deleted, update both the head position and the new head's prev pointer.

Time: O(1)
Auxiliary Space: O(1)



/*
// Definition for a Node.
class ListNode {
    public int data;
    public ListNode prev;
    public ListNode next;
    public ListNode();
    public ListNode(int data);
    public ListNode(int data, ListNode prev, ListNode next);
};
*/
class Solution {
    public ListNode deleteHead(ListNode head) {

        // Empty list
        if (head == null) {
            return null;
        }

        // Only one node
        if (head.next == null) {
            return null;
        }

        // Move head to the second node
        head = head.next;

        // Remove the backward connection
        head.prev = null;

        // Return the new head
        return head;
    }
}
